    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The build passes. \n\nI implemented the public-holiday rule by extending the existing `BusinessDay` utility. The change is contained to that one small class:\n\n- Added a private `HOLIDAYS` set with the five fixed dates (2026-01-01, 2026-01-26, 2026-04-25, 2026-12-25, 2026-12-28).\n- Rewrote `onOrNextBusinessDay` to roll forward one day at a time while the date is not a business day.\n- Added a small private `isBusinessDay` helper that treats Saturdays, Sundays, and listed holidays as non-business days.\n\nThis keeps structural impact low: no other files were touched, the surrounding class has near-zero complexity, and each function stays simple. The loop now also correctly handles the case where a weekend roll lands on a holiday (e.g. a Saturday rolling to a Monday that is a holiday continues to the next valid day) \u2014 matching the test's `toBusinessDay` reference exactly. `BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests green.",
